- Consider all 1P & 3P resources as context associated to this project, even if not explicitly linked.
- Start from this object as the root. You may follow at most one hop of links from these pages (e.g., linked Jira issues, Confluence pages, JPD ideas, or Slack threads) only if the linked resource clearly refers back to this project (by name, ID, or direct context)
- A reminder qualifies only if it directly advances this workstream. Exclude items from other workstreams that merely share a meeting or author. Formatting rules: Format it for fast scanability
- H2. Reminders
- List only action items I am responsible for, if any.
- Find any actions I need to follow up on. Could be actual tasks assigned to me, comments I'm tagged in but haven't responded to, or things I said I would do in a conversation or meeting.
- Each reminder MUST start with the ballot box with tick emoji (☑️) and MUST NOT be a bulleted list.
- For each reminder, use:
☑️ Action (short)
When: (date/timeframe if known)
Context: (1 sentence)
Link: (URL) General rules:
- Use markdown headings and bolding for structure.
- Include links wherever relevant.
- If there are no reminders, write "No new reminders."`,description:'Prompt sent to Rovo Chat when the user clicks "Find my action items" on a space surface. Do not translate the formatting instructions or emoji characters.'},prepForCheckinTitle:{id:"ai-mate.rovo-spaces.starters.prep-for-checkin-title.nonFinal",defaultMessage:"Prep for check-in meeting",description:"Title of the prep for check-in meeting chat starter shown in Rovo empty chat state"},prepForCheckinPrompt:{id:"ai-mate.rovo-spaces.starters.prep-for-checkin-prompt",defaultMessage:`I have a weekly sync starting soon for this workstream. Prep a brief agenda, including:
1. Highlights from the last week. Include 1-4. Can cover momentum, milestones, decisions, risks, learnings. Use emoji for each.
